  "description": "These Tex-Mex peppers sport a cheesy, creamy beef-and-rice filling that's spiked with chili powder and cumin. They're topped with an enchilada-style sauce and gets its depth from ancho chile and unsweetened cocoa powders and its aromatics from cumin and lightly floral Mexican oregano.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: red bell peppers → yellow bell peppers or orange bell peppers\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The filling can be prepared in advance, and the peppers may be stuffed ahead of time. The same is true of the sauce; however, store the two components separately in the refrigerator. Remove the peppers and sauce from the refrigerator about 45 minutes before cooking to bring them to room temperature.",
  "author": [
    "Jennifer Olvera"
